## Class diagram (backend layers)

```mermaid
classDiagram
    class BaseEntity {
        +Long id
        +LocalDateTime createdAt
        +LocalDateTime updatedAt
    }
    BaseEntity <|-- User
    BaseEntity <|-- Restaurant
    BaseEntity <|-- FoodItem
    BaseEntity <|-- Order
    BaseEntity <|-- DeliveryAgent

    class FoodItem {
        +int stockCount
        +int lowStockThreshold
        +Availability availability
        +refreshAvailability()
        +reduceStock(int)
        +restoreStock(int)
    }

    class Order {
        +OrderStatus status
        +int priorityScore
        +Integer manualPriority
        +effectivePriority() int
        +totalPrepTime() int
    }

    class OrderService {
        +placeOrder()
        +updateStatus()
        +cancelOrder()
        +smartQueue()
    }
    class PriorityService {
        +calculateScore(Order) int
        +buildQueue(List~Order~) List~Order~
    }
    class RecommendationService {
        +personalised(customerId) List
        +frequentlyBoughtTogether(foodId) List
        +recordOrder(Order)
    }
    class DeliveryService {
        +assignAgent(Order)
        +advance(orderId, status)
    }

    OrderService --> PriorityService
    OrderService --> RecommendationService
    OrderService --> DeliveryService
    OrderService --> FoodItem
```

Layering to show: `Controller → Service → Repository (Spring Data JPA) → MySQL`, with DTOs
crossing the controller boundary and entities staying inside the service layer.

